# Network Data Structures (common crate)

Rust library for storing and representing parsed network frame data (L2-L4).

## Architecture

- `net_common.rs` — all struct/enum definitions
- `impls.rs` — constructors, helper methods, Default impls
- `display.rs` — fmt::Display implementations

## Naming Conventions

- Structs: `PascalCase` with domain prefixes where appropriate: `EthData`, `IpData`, `MplsData`
- Enums: `PascalCase`, variants without `Snake_Case` — use `PascalCase`
- Allow `non_snake_case`, `non_camel_case_types` for network-standard names (e.g., `TLV_DATA`, `CDP_CISCO_DATA`)
- Constants: `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE`, prefixed by domain: `BROADCAST_ADDRESS6`, `LLDP_TLV_MAX_LEN`

## Data Patterns

- Address types wrap fixed arrays: `MacAddr6([u8; 6])`, `Ipv4Addr { octets: [u8; 4] }`
- IP variant enum: `IpAddr::V4(Ipv4Addr)` / `IpAddr::V6(Ipv6Addr)`
- Payload hierarchy: `NetData` → `EthData` + `NetPayload` enum
- Protocol errors stored in `ParseError` enum with context fields (len, src, dst)
- Fixed-size TLV buffers: `TLV_DATA` with `LLDP_TLV_MAX_LEN`

## Adding New Protocol Support

1. Define structs in `net_common.rs`
2. Add variant to `NetPayload` enum
3. Add variant to `ParseError` if needed
4. Add constructor in `impls.rs`
5. Add `fmt::Display` in `display.rs`

## Style Rules

- `Copy + Clone` on all small data structs (no heap allocations in frame data)
- `Default` impl for all data types
- `#[repr(C, packed)]` only for wire-format headers (e.g., `CISCO_CDP_HEADER`)
- `use crate::net_common::*;` in other modules
- Comments in Russian for domain-specific notes, English for RFC references
